# tcrsift canonical TCR constant-region AA sequences (single-allele defaults).
#
# This file is the runtime source for the module-level constants
# `HUMAN_TRAC_AA`, `HUMAN_TRBC1_AA`, `HUMAN_TRBC2_AA` (and the dict
# `HUMAN_CONSTANT_REGIONS_AA`). See `canonical_constants_alleles.fasta`
# for the per-allele references used by the auto-detect picker added
# in 2.3 (#113).
#
# Defaults:
#   - TRAC*01 (the only widely-referenced TRAC allele)
#   - TRBC1*01 (the major TRBC1 allele)
#   - TRBC2*01 — the major TRBC2 allele in human populations.
#     Pre-2.3 shipped TRBC2*03 (the Ensembl/UniProt entry) which has
#     K at mature position 9; ~99% of humans carry E at that position
#     (TRBC2*01). #113 audit on B1-2/B1-3 showed both donors uniformly
#     TRBC2*01.
#
# All three sequences are BARE MATURE protein. The J→C junction
# residue is read per-clone from the CellRanger contig at assembly
# time — see _add_constant_regions in assemble.py and #105.

>TRAC|UniProt:P01848|Ensembl:ENST00000611116|release:110|allele:01
IQNPDPAVYQLRDSKSSDKSVCLFTDFDSQTNVSQSKDSDVYITDKTVLDMRSMDFKSNS
AVAWSNKSDFACANAFNNSIIPEDTFFPSPESSCDVKLVEKSFETDTNLNFQNLSVIGFR
ILLLKVAGFNLLMTLRLWSS

